      "writtenOn": "2025-12-15T09:52:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Why do we need to clone the expectation instead of just checking that the buffer content is the same as the readback buffer? It seems that we have some complexity because we try to use the deferred expectation mechanism to check the contents of the replayed buffers. Instead we could on TearDown first handle all the deferred expectations, save the buffer contents on the side, and then only after that, do the replay, and manually copy and map buffers to check their contents.\n\nThe alternative if you really want to use the same expectations, would be to make them stored as a shared_ptr instead of a unique_ptr. (but imho it is a bit more intrusive compared to manual expectation just for replay as suggested above).",
      "revId": "eb105d894a44d5097e0f9a6971fdafbdabe0a07e",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
